  "_approach": "Classic EDM-adjacent snare-roll build on a 32nd grid over the house 4x4: bar 1 keeps the kick/clap/offbeat-hat bounce (bh_night_bass_bounce) while the snare enters in soft 8ths; bar 2 drops the kick entirely and the snare tightens through a 16th roll into a full 32nd roll ramping to 127, with the open hat swelling underneath and the last three 32nds left silent — the silence before the drop. Ref: EDMProd's build-up guide (8th->16th->32nd snare density progression), MusicRadar's ultimate snare-roll build-up, Point Blank's \"make your drops hit harder\" silence-gap technique.",
